asset:        filmagic-timeline.png
title:        README: timeline and loudness detail
author:       Filmagic contributors (screenshot); film/footage/music credits below
source:       original work (screenshot of Filmagic captured with its ui.screenshot control command)
license:      MIT OR Apache-2.0 (screenshot); embedded film frames are public domain, music CC0-1.0
license-file:
added:        2026-11-12 by @vansyson1308
notes:        Crop (2200x849 px at 2x) of the Timeline and Audio Meters panels, captured 0.8 s after playback started 24.7 s into the Trailer sequence, so the meters are live: Night of the Living Dead shots with dissolves on V1 and their sound on A1, the Carnival of Souls insert on V2, the Chopin nocturne waveform on A2, coloured markers on the ruler, the selected clip outlined, and the BS.1770 loudness readout (M, S, I, TP). All UI icons are drawn in code; fonts are Inter and JetBrains Mono (OFL-1.1). Contains no Adobe artwork. Rebuild and recapture with the scripts in docs/images/scripts/ (README there): build_trailer.py, then capture_gallery.py timeline.
Media visible or used in the screenshot (none of it is committed to the repository):
  - Night of the Living Dead (1968), dir. George A. Romero, Image Ten. US public domain (released without a copyright notice). Source: https://archive.org/details/night-of-the-living-dead-1968-english (Public Domain Mark).
  - Carnival of Souls (1962), dir. Herk Harvey, Harcourt Productions. US public domain. Source: https://archive.org/details/CarnivalOfSoulsVideoQualityUpgrade (Public Domain Mark).
  - Chopin, Nocturne Op. 48 No. 1, performed for Musopen. CC0-1.0. Source: https://archive.org/details/musopen-chopin (shown only as a waveform).
